# Bootstrap only: every route (the dashboard's own domain included) is pushed by the agent through
# the admin API, so this file must not declare sites — a site block here would take :80/:443 and
# collide with the server the agent creates. Caddy runs with --resume, so the routes written by the
# admin API survive restarts and this file is used only on the very first boot.
#
# The admin API listens on a unix socket shared with the agent alone: on a TCP port it would also be
# reachable by the deployed application containers, which share the 'zydock' network with the proxy.
{
	admin unix//var/run/caddy/admin.sock
}
